  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the patient self-report ASA engine. calculateASA(state) evaluates the 42 declarative rules in catalogue order (CV, RS, RN, HP, EN, NR, HM, OB, FC, AG, SH) and returns { asaGrade = max grade of fired rules (1 when none), firedRules }. Split engine: form-app.js first runs recomputeDerived() (demographics.bmi = round1(weight/height^2), functionalCapacity.estimatedMETs from exerciseTolerance - the persona states carry those derived values pre-filled and consistent), then calls detectAdditionalFlags(state) separately, so flags are pinned as expected.additionalFlags with flagsArgs [\"state\"]; the detector pushes in source order then stable-sorts high > medium > low. Quirks verified: AG-001 (age > 80) derives age from the frozen wall clock (2026-09-03), so a patient born exactly 80 years earlier is silent; CV-003 (stable IHD) is suppressed whenever recentMI is 'yes' while CV-004 needs recentMIWeeks < 12, so IHD with an MI 12+ weeks ago fires NO cardiovascular rule even though FLAG-CARDIAC-002 still fires on recentMI alone; HP-001 is likewise suppressed by cirrhosis 'yes' and COPD / diabetes / cirrhosis with a blank severity / control / Child-Pugh field fire nothing; OB-001 needs bmi >= 30 (29.8 is silent) and FC-001 needs METs < 4 ('climb-stairs' = 4 is silent); anaphylaxis flags are indexed by allergy array position and every non-empty allergy list adds FLAG-ALLERGY-001. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas pre-operative-assessment-by-patient --update",
